{%- comment -%}
  Newsletter modal, shown once after a delay on the visitor's first look around.

  Design note: the store's signature device is the hazard-tape stripe, so the
  dialog is edged with it rather than given a gradient or a stock photo. One
  brand button, charcoal type, nothing else competing — the CTA is the only
  flare on screen while it is open.

  Behaviour (mts-theme.js):
    · fires after `delay` seconds, first visit only
    · dismissal remembered for `snooze` days; a successful signup is permanent
    · never appears on the cart or checkout, where it would interrupt a purchase
    · Esc and backdrop close it; focus is trapped and returned
    · honours prefers-reduced-motion
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if settings.popup_enabled -%}
  <div class="mts-pop" data-mts-popup
       data-delay="{{ settings.popup_delay | default: 10 }}"
       data-snooze="{{ settings.popup_snooze | default: 30 }}"
       role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="mts-pop-title" hidden>
    <div class="mts-pop__scrim" data-mts-popup-close></div>

    <div class="mts-pop__card">
      <button class="mts-pop__close" data-mts-popup-close aria-label="Close">
        {% render 'mts-icon', name: 'close', size: 18 %}
      </button>

      <div class="mts-pop__body">
        {%- comment -%}
          The brand mark does the job the old "TRADE LIST" eyebrow was doing —
          saying who this is from — and does it faster and with more authority
          than a small caps label. Left-aligned so it anchors the same optical
          edge as the headline beneath it.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <a class="mts-pop__logo" href="{{ routes.root_url }}" aria-label="{{ shop.name }}">
          {%- if settings.logo != blank -%}
            <img src="{{ settings.logo | image_url: width: 392 }}" alt="{{ shop.name }}" width="168" height="29">
          {%- else -%}
            <img src="{{ 'mts-logo.png' | asset_url }}" alt="{{ shop.name }}" width="168" height="29">
          {%- endif -%}
        </a>

        {%- comment -%}
          Deliberately NOT an <h2>. This popup renders on every page of the
          store, so as a real heading it injected the same H2 — "First look at
          new lines and price breaks." — into the outline of every URL on the
          site, competing with each page's actual H2s in any SEO audit.

          role="heading" aria-level="2" keeps it a heading for assistive tech
          and still labels the dialog through aria-labelledby, but it is no
          longer part of the document's heading structure for crawlers.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <p class="mts-pop__title" id="mts-pop-title" role="heading" aria-level="2">
          {{ settings.popup_title | default: 'First look at new lines and price breaks.' }}
        </p>

        <p class="mts-pop__text">
          {{ settings.popup_text | default: 'Join the trade list for new stock, bulk pricing and the occasional job-site tip. No spam, unsubscribe anytime.' }}
        </p>

        {%- form 'customer', class: 'mts-pop__formwrap', id: 'mts-popup-form' -%}
          {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
            <p class="mts-pop__done" data-mts-popup-success>
              {% render 'mts-icon', name: 'check', size: 18 %}
              You're on the list — check your inbox.
            </p>
          {%- else -%}
            <input type="hidden" name="contact[tags]" value="newsletter, popup">
            <div class="mts-pop__form">
              <input type="email" name="contact[email]" required
                     placeholder="you@company.com.au" aria-label="Email address"
                     autocomplete="email">
              <button class="btn btn--brand btn--lg" type="submit">
                {{ settings.popup_cta | default: 'Join the list' }}
              </button>
            </div>
            {%- if form.errors -%}
              <p class="mts-pop__fine" role="alert">{{ form.errors | default_errors }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endform -%}

        <p class="mts-pop__fine">
          {% render 'mts-icon', name: 'lock', size: 12 %}
          We never share your address.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
